            <ArticleTitle>Intraoperative coronary artery spasm after off-pump coronary surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>614-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0218492313480356</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery spasm is rare after coronary artery bypass surgery. We describe a case of intraoperative severe native coronary artery and graft spasm after successful off-pump coronary bypass surgery in a 55-year-old man, which was detected by suspicious electrocardiographic changes, and documented postoperatively by coronary angiography.</AbstractText>
